cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the AI Chip Fab Atlas, please cite the version you used and its
  evidence cutoff date. For statements about an individual campus, also cite
  the underlying public sources recorded in the Atlas.
type: dataset
title: "AI Chip Fab Atlas: Public-Evidence Atlas of AI-Relevant Chip-Fabrication Campuses"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
authors:
  - name: Berkeley AI Risk
    website: "https://ai-risk.berkeley.edu"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Berkeley-AI-Risk/ai-chip-fab-atlas"
url: "https://github.com/Berkeley-AI-Risk/ai-chip-fab-atlas"
abstract: >-
  A public-evidence inventory of 31 physical wafer-fabrication campuses that may
  matter for advanced AI chips, with a cited coordinate, an attributed aerial or
  satellite image, and claim-level evidence on each campus's identity,
  lifecycle, fabrication capability, and publicly reported AI-chip products.
  Evidence reviewed through August 25, 2026. The Atlas was compiled by AI agents
  under human direction as an experiment in AI-assisted open-source
  intelligence gathering and documentation.
keywords:
  - semiconductor fabrication
  - AI chips
  - AI governance
  - open-source intelligence
  - OSINT
  - dataset
